### Step 6 — Review

Three questions are read at every rigor — `evidence` · `adversarial` · `structure` — each by the one independent reader `SKILL.md`'s rigor table deals it. The auditor falsifies the *evidence* and never reviews the code; the critic and the reviewer falsify the *code*. A reader is never the author nor a fork of the orchestrator, and is shown no other reader's verdict. Its brief names its questions on a line of its own, `Questions: <q>[, <q>]`, exactly the set the plan's rigor deals its role, or the dispatch wall refuses it; and nothing of their checks: `payload/context/checks-<question>.md` is delivered to it at start, and a paraphrase is a weaker second source.

**Each landing is read.** A read row is a `review` row whose `reads` carries `live:head:<q>[+<q>]`; exclusivity, range and return-to-pending are per question. It is ready for each landed difference its questions have not read, and its reader reads that range (`scope: piece`).

**The whole read, once.** At `scale: wave` each code question also owes `scope=whole`, read once the last build row has landed, in the one batch `steps/5.md` dispatches; it reads across pieces, never each piece again.

**The read after a fix.** A fix gets one read per owed question, over the range the tick prints for its row and the plan rows and criteria it names. A row confirmed at an earlier head and not named is not read again.

**The record and its fact.** A reader writes one file under `record/` with flush-left lines `reviewed: <a>..<b>`, `question: <q>`, `result: <pass|flag|fail>`, `scope: <piece|whole>`; for `structure`, one line `check: <id> <PASS|FLAG|FAIL|n/a> <reason>` per check id. Register it with `session-poker.sh proof-add review <record> --question <q> --reader <name>`: the head is the record's `b`; the reader's role is read from its roster row, never typed. Code past a question's last head is uncovered for that question.

**The waiver is the user's.** `session-poker.sh waive <question> '<reply>'` writes `waived: question=<q> head=<40-hex> by <git user.name> <ISO-UTC> "<reason>"`, covering that question up to that head. An agent never waives.
